== landing  A's fix (63bbc33), measured, facts and checks, no proposal (no gate): gears.landing foresees a landing from the part's globals before and after, and swbuild.update_variables sets the change by way of the nearest safe tooth count, two rebuilds. On fresh copies of S0's master's parts or of parts built here from scratch, nothing saved, every document closed: (1) routed as the app stands; (2) the threshold: the same set straight (swbuild.LANDING_STEPS patched to () in this process, restored), with two external gears, then the externals routed; (3) changes that land nothing, one rebuild; (4) a module change with a tooth change; (5) the straight failure closed unsaved and reopened; and the fixes review's cases (c997e85): (6) just above 0.2, unrouted and clean; (7) the old end past the new start (ring m1 36 -> 34) and one well clear; (8) recipe B, never routed, its dimension links read; (9) a module-only landing, by way of 54 and back; (10) a user's own feature in error on a routed part. Each straight case reads the short solved line's ends before and after. A FAIL only where a routed result is not clean or not as foreseen, or a document is left open or saved
